{
 "note": "Maps every bed and cue name in the cue sheet (out/cuesheet.json from tools/cuesheet.js, or audio/cues_draft.json until it exists) to sound. Cues: rel_db is the sound's loudest 100 ms (K-weighted) relative to the narration's integrated loudness, so every effect sits under the voice (the author wants few, quiet effects); align peak puts the sound's loudest point on the cue time (impacts, whooshes at the cut), start puts its onset there; pan -1..1 (a cue's own p.pan wins); cycle rotates files by occurrence; steps lays a cue's p.n steps at its p.gap; per_n_s makes a cue's length p.n x per_n_s (typing); a cue's p.gain_db or p.level adds to rel_db. Beds: music beds map, sequence by sequence, to a variation in audio/score_plan.json beds (a list splits one engine bed at spoken words: `until` a phrase, the next segment `from` it); null is silent on purpose. aliases map other names. Same-name cues closer than 150 ms play once.",
 "mix": {
  "target_lufs": -14.0,
  "true_peak_ceiling_dbtp": -1.5,
  "music_under_voice_db": 12.0,
  "speech_gap_merge_s": 1.2,
  "duck_attack_s": 0.35,
  "duck_release_s": 0.9,
  "presence_dip_db": 3.0,
  "presence_hz": 2500,
